•
no reaction between bromine and potassium chloride / reaction mixture
remains an orange colour / no colour change;
•
because chlorine is more reactive than bromine ORA;
•
solution goes brown with potassium iodide / solution darkens with
potassium iodide;
•
there is a reaction with potassium iodide / potassium bromide formed with
potassium iodide / bromine formed with potassium iodide;
•
iodine less reactive than bromine ORA;
